  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Triangle round – the goalkeeper faces three angles in a row",
  "description": "Half the court, goalkeeper in goal. Four spots: B and C by each board level with the centre line, D in the corner next to the goal and the shooter A in the other corner. B, C and D have balls. A comes out of the corner, gets a pass from B and shoots. Then A backs out to the top of the slot, gets a pass from C and shoots again. Finally A moves across to the other side, gets the pass from D and shoots a third time.\n\nThe goalkeeper resets to a new angle before every shot. Rotate: A to B's spot, B to C, C to D and D becomes the new shooter. Switch sides after a few minutes so both left- and right-handed shooters shoot from both sides.\n\nVariant: the passers choose the order themselves, so the goalkeeper does not know where the next shot is coming from. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: move while the pass is travelling and be still when the shot is taken."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: read the passer and the shooter's blade – it shows where the shot is going."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: shoot first time or off the first touch, and give the goalkeeper a new angle every time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Passers: wait until the goalkeeper has reset before the next pass."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
